hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"210","On dower: [Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Suwayd ibn Manjuf] narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah; he heard Abdullah ibn Kulayb al-Sadusi [narrating], from Yahya ibn Ya'mar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make the private parts of women lawful to you with the best of your wealth."
"211","Isa ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Damrah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Bakr, from Makhul, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever makes the private part lawful, whether a gift or present, counts as part of the dower."
"212","Harun ibn Zayd ibn Abi al-Zarqa narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad - meaning Ibn Rashid - narrated to us, from Makhul, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever makes the forbidden lawful, whether a gift or a promise, belongs to her; and the most deserving of what a man honors is his daughter [and his sister]. Abu Dawud said: [Something similar has been narrated with a connected chain]."
"213","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Ja'far, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Muhammad ibn Thawban, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever uncovers a woman and looks at her private parts, the dower becomes due."
"214","Hannad narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Umayr al-Khath'ami, from Abd al-Malik ibn al-Mughirah al-Ta'ifi, from Ibn al-Baylamani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: (And give women their dowries as a gift). They said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the ties between them? He said: Whatever their families mutually agree upon."
